Implement the declared Cott contract deterministically.
Iterate CottList; Option: test Some then direct else; final union variant direct; fail closed.
The project lock selects psycopg with its binary extra. PostgreSQL operations use its real psycopg APIs; network and database effects permit those SDK calls without an invented Cott adapter.
Use only scoped declared facade functions for Cott composition. Never import private implementations or retain mutable global connection state.
Connection credentials are data, never SQL text or shell commands. Preserve authenticated TLS and SSH host-key checks; map genuine operation failures to declared errors without leaking credentials.
cott-domain real.pgcli.resolve_credential return: Credential resolution uses the lock-selected keyring package and the standard-library getpass module. The file.read/file.write effects cover terminal input and prompt output; never fall back to echoed password input or modify stored credentials.
cott-domain real.pgcli.connect return: Fully parameterize subprocess.Popen[str] and CompletedProcess[str] annotations for text-mode subprocesses; an unparameterized Popen makes stdout text Unknown. Preserve real SSH readiness and cleanup; no suppressions.
cott-domain real.pgcli.execute_planned_query return: psycopg.connect rejects expansion of dict[str,str] into its overload-specific kwargs. Build the libpq conninfo string with psycopg.conninfo.make_conninfo and pass it positionally, with explicit autocommit/row_factory options. Execute intentionally user-supplied whole SQL as UTF-8 bytes; fixed SQL helper parameters use LiteralString. Error.diag is not optional. Explicitly type memoryview[int] before byte conversion. Preserve behavior; do not cast away errors.
cott-domain real.pgcli.export_query return: Build libpq conninfo with psycopg.conninfo.make_conninfo rather than expanding dict[str,str] into psycopg.connect; pass autocommit explicitly. User-provided complete SQL may be encoded to UTF-8 bytes; fixed SQL literals retain LiteralString typing. psycopg.Error.diag is nonoptional. No suppressions.
cott-domain real.pgcli.import_delimited return: Build libpq conninfo with psycopg.conninfo.make_conninfo, pass it positionally to psycopg.connect, and set autocommit explicitly; never expand dict[str,str] into overload-specific kwargs. psycopg.Error.diag is nonoptional. Preserve parameterized data loading and rollback.
cott-domain real.pgcli.load_favorites return: JSON decoding produces object data. After isinstance(list/dict), cast to list[object] or dict[object,object] before iteration or len; then validate each key/value and nested tag. Do not iterate list[Unknown], dict[Unknown,Unknown] or untyped object-pairs. Keep the strict persisted format and duplicate-name rejection.
cott-domain real.pgcli.load_history return: JSON decoding produces object data. After isinstance(list/dict), cast to list[object] or dict[object,object] before len/keys/items/indexing; then validate every field before constructing HistoryEntry. Bool is not a timestamp integer. No Unknown container variables or suppressions.
cott-domain real.pgcli.receive_notifications return: Build libpq conninfo with psycopg.conninfo.make_conninfo and pass it positionally to psycopg.connect; use explicit autocommit=True, not arbitrary dict[str,str] expansion. Preserve real bounded notification reads and resource cleanup.
cott-domain real.pgcli.refresh_catalog return: Build libpq conninfo with psycopg.conninfo.make_conninfo and pass it positionally to psycopg.connect with explicit autocommit. Fixed SQL helper arguments are LiteralString; use real parameterized metadata queries, not general str query annotations. No suppressions.
cott-domain real.pgcli.resolve_connection_plan return: psycopg.conninfo.conninfo_to_dict returns dict[str,ConnParam], where ConnParam includes str, int and None. Preserve its actual inferred type or annotate Mapping[str,str|int|None]; explicitly narrow/convert each value when populating string ConnectionSettings. Never force an invariant dict[str,str|None] annotation onto it.
cott-domain real.pgcli.run return: Use psycopg.conninfo.make_conninfo to build connection data, then pass it positionally to psycopg.connect with explicit autocommit/connect_timeout. The deliberately user-authored whole SQL command can be UTF-8 bytes for Cursor.execute. Never pass a generic str as LiteralString or expand dict[str,str] into overload-specific connection kwargs. The exported Cott Never return annotation is exactly typing.Never, not typing.NoReturn; preserve that runtime annotation identity.
cott-domain real.pgcli.run_interactive return: Use psycopg.conninfo.make_conninfo rather than dict[str,str] expansion into psycopg.connect. Normalize decoded JSON and nested list/dict values to typed object containers with cast before iterating; validate elements before converting to strings or joining. Do not propagate Unknown from favorites or result rendering. Preserve all existing real operations and error behavior.
cott-domain real.pgcli.run_meta_command return: Build conninfo using psycopg.conninfo.make_conninfo and pass explicit connection options. Narrow raw list/dict values through typed object containers before iteration, join or string conversion. Do not leave list[Unknown] or dict[Unknown,Unknown] values; preserve real commands rather than substituting errors.
cott-domain real.pgcli.save_favorites return: Inputs already have checked Favorite/Str/U64 ABI types; do not repeat tautological isinstance tests on them. Validate nonempty unique names, capacity and filesystem conditions. An error-return helper must return Err[ClientError], not invariant Err[ClientError_FavoriteFailed], so it composes with Result[Unit,ClientError]. No casts or suppressions to erase canonical result types.
cott-domain real.pgcli.watch_query return: Build libpq conninfo with psycopg.conninfo.make_conninfo and pass it positionally to psycopg.connect with explicit autocommit. psycopg.Error.diag is nonoptional. Preserve bounded real executions, intervals and cleanup.
cott-domain real.pgcli.connect error: _path_opt only receives the concrete Path fields of TlsSettings, so annotate its argument pathlib.Path and use str(value), not object plus isinstance(os.PathLike) (unparameterized PathLike introduces Unknown).
cott-domain real.pgcli.execute_planned_query error: isinstance(value,memoryview) narrows to memoryview[Unknown]; an annotated assignment alone does not remove Unknown. Explicitly cast(memoryview[int], value) before assigning the local view, then convert to bytes.
cott-domain real.pgcli.save_favorites error: os.fspath(store.path) is statically str because store.path is pathlib.Path; remove the redundant isinstance(path,str) condition. Keep the meaningful empty/path/filesystem validation.
